{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "item_manipulation",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "Manipulating items with a multi-limb robot: pick an item up, put it down where the gripper stands or carry it somewhere first, stop whatever is in flight, and report what is held.",
      "Each action is a whole sequence, planned and carried out by the implementer, and returns a result when the sequence ends. They sit above limb_motion, whose moves command one limb at a time and carry no knowledge of what the limb is reaching for. Finding an item is item_perception's job; the identifier it mints is what grab_item takes.",
      "Every pose and point, commanded or reported, is the gripper's grasp point and names its frame and its time: a goal's target in any frame of the robot's tree, a result's final_point in the robot frame. A pose is the gripper's grasp point, the same convention item_perception reports an item's pose in. Grippers are named from the implementer's fixed set of gripper names, which get_state lists.",
      "The robot frame is the robot frame of transforms: the root link of the robot's URDF.",
      "Each grab_item and place_item goal that names a target names its frame and its time: the target is a pose in a frame as transforms names frames, at a timestamp on the clock of transforms. A command with no frame lies in the robot frame. When it accepts a goal, the implementer places the target by its tree at its timestamp, as transforms defines a lookup: a target in the robot frame with the timestamp of a report names where the robot frame stood then. A command with no timestamp is placed by the latest transforms when the implementer accepts it; a target in the robot frame with no timestamp names where the robot frame stands then. A goal whose target the implementer cannot place is refused with the failure kind of the lookup, its message naming the cause as transform_lookup's does. An orientation whose squared norm lies 0.01 or more from 1 is refused with `rejected`, the tolerance of tf2's buffer that transforms names; the implementer normalizes each orientation it takes. These refusals are the only ones of this contract that refuse the goal; every other refusal is in the result.",
      "A target's position says where and is always required. Its orientation says how. A target with no orientation leaves the orientation to the implementer, so a caller never has to invent a quaternion it does not mean.",
      "One sequence at a time. A goal that arrives while another sequence is running is refused and the running sequence continues untouched; the refusal names the running action. A caller that wants the robot regardless aborts first. This is what keeps two callers, an operator and an autonomous planner among them, from interleaving sequences on one robot.",
      "abort is the one goal admitted while a sequence is running: it stops that sequence and returns once the robot has come to rest, standing where the stop left it. A cancel on a running goal's own handle stops the robot the same way; the two differ only in who may issue them, since a cancel is available only to the caller holding the handle while abort is a goal in its own right that any caller can issue. abort never appears as current_action in get_state, and abort against an idle robot succeeds and reports that no sequence was running.",
      "grab_item, drop_item and place_item have the mark `moves_robot`, and abort and get_state have no mark: each MCP server, `peppy node call` and each lease holder asks the daemon (`robot_leases.check_move`) whether it may move the robot before it calls one of the three, so an abort never waits for a lease.",
      "An item identifier comes from item_perception's identify_item, or is minted here when grab_item takes an item addressed by pose, and names that one item for as long as the implementer can still account for it. An identifier the implementer no longer recognises is refused in the result. Identifiers are opaque: callers compare them and pass them back, and read nothing into their text.",
      "A gripper's held flag is set when grab_item succeeds on it and cleared when drop_item or place_item succeeds on it. A refused, failed, cancelled, or aborted sequence leaves the flag as it was. The flag follows results, not the jaws: a sequence stopped partway can leave the gripper holding what the flag does not report, or the reverse, and the flag stays as it was until a later grab_item, drop_item, or place_item succeeds. get_state reports the flag, and beside it the opening of each gripper as the implementer last measured it: an item that slips out of the jaws after grab_item succeeded leaves the flag set and the opening near 0.",
      "The fields that hold an item identifier have the mark `item_id` (marks.json5). The workflow side reads it: a workflow passes an item identifier only from a field with the same mark of a result or an observation of the same node instance, never as a literal. grab_item also has the mark `reaches_for_item`: a workflow that calls it first checks that the robot reaches its work zone, or the item, with a call of a member whose result has a field with the mark `checks_reach`, such as check_positions of workspace, on the point of the item.",
      "grab_item, drop_item and place_item report their sequence in their feedback: one message at the start of each stage, which names the stage, says in one sentence what the robot does now, and gives the number and the maximum of a stage that repeats. Each part of a sequence in which the robot can stand still for more than 1 s is a stage of its own, so the person who looks at a robot that does not move can read why. A goal refused before it starts gives no feedback, and abort gives none. The sentence is in the field activity, which has the mark `activity` (marks.json5): the workflow side shows it to the person who follows a run.",
    ],
  },
  failure_kinds: {
    unknown_frame: "A frame of the request is named by no transform the implementer has received that passed the checks of transforms",
    no_chain: "A frame of the request and the frame the implementer places it in are in trees that share no frame",
    extrapolation: "A moving transform on the chain has no value at the request's time: the implementer holds no stamp of it, or the time is before the oldest stamp it holds of it or after its newest",
    broken_tree: "A frame whose transform to its parent the chain needs has transforms from two publishers, or the chain runs through a cycle",
  },
  interfaces: {
    actions: [
      {
        name: "grab_item",
        description: "Pick an item up with one gripper: the implementer reaches the item, named by its item_id or by a grasp pose, and closes the gripper on it. The feedback gives each stage of the grab as it starts: plan, while the jaws open for the item and the implementer looks for a path to it; move_above, the move of the gripper to the point above the item; with a model that aligns the gripper, align_look, each question to that model, and align_move, each correction of the gripper that an answer gives, each with its number; then grasp, the descent, the close of the jaws and the lift. The result tells whether the grasp succeeded, and names the gripper that now holds the item and the identifier of the item. All other fields except action_time are zero or empty when success is false.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            gripper_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Which gripper closes on the item, named from the implementer's fixed set of gripper names (e.g. \"left_gripper\"). An unknown name is refused in the result, as is a gripper that already holds an item. Empty leaves the choice to the implementer, which picks a free gripper suited to the item's position and is refused in the result when none is free. The result names the gripper that took the item either way." },
            item_id: { $type: "string", $marks: ["item_id"], $description: "Identifier of an item item_perception's identify_item found. Empty hands the target to the implementer instead, so a caller that already knows where to reach needs no identify_item first. An identifier the implementer no longer recognises is refused in the result." },
            target: {
              $type: "object",
              $description: "The grasp-point pose to take the item at, given in frame at timestamp. Read only when item_id is empty; a goal that names an item_id sends a zero position here, with no frame, no timestamp and no orientation. A target with no orientation leaves the orientation to the implementer: it approaches the position however it judges best, the same freedom it has when the goal names an item_id instead.",
              frame: { $type: "string", $optional: true, $description: "The frame of the record's values, as transforms names frames; absent, the robot frame." },
              timestamp: { $type: "time", $optional: true, $description: "The time on the clock of transforms at which the values hold. A command leaves it out for the latest time; a report leaves it out for values that hold at every time." },
              position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "x, y, z (m)." },
              orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $optional: true, $description: "A unit quaternion [x, y, z, w], or absent for none." },
            },
            max_effort: { $type: "f64", $description: "Maximum effort the gripper may exert closing on the item (magnitude, in the gripper's effort unit). 0 = no preference; the implementer's configured ceiling applies." },
          },
        },
        feedback_topic: {
          qos_profile: "reliable",
          message_format: {
            stage: { $type: "string", $enum: ["plan", "move_above", "align_look", "align_move", "grasp"], $description: "The stage that starts now, as the description of the action names it." },
            activity: { $type: "string", $marks: ["activity"], $description: "One sentence for the person who looks at the robot: what the robot does now, in the words of what that person sees (the robot, its arm, its hand, each item by its label), with no name of a link, a joint, a contract or a model and no term of the motion planner. A stage that repeats ends the sentence with its number and its maximum, as \"(2 of 5)\", so the sentence alone tells one repeat from the next." },
            number: { $type: "u32", $description: "The number of this repeat of a stage that repeats, from 1. For align_look and align_move, the step of the alignment, which a question to the model and the correction that its answer gives share: a step whose answer moves nothing gives no align_move. 0 for a stage that does not repeat." },
            maximum: { $type: "u32", $description: "How many times the stage can repeat in this goal: for align_look and align_move, the steps of the alignment. 0 for a stage that does not repeat." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            success: { $type: "bool", $description: "False when the grasp was refused, failed, cancelled, or aborted; message says which. Refused before reaching when another sequence is running, the named gripper is unknown or already holds an item, no gripper is free for a goal that named none, or the item_id is one the implementer no longer recognises." },
            message: "string",
            gripper_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Gripper that now holds the item, from the implementer's fixed set of gripper names. It repeats the goal's name, or names the one the implementer chose when the goal left it empty, so the caller knows which gripper to address with drop_item or place_item." },
            item_id: { $type: "string", $marks: ["item_id"], $description: "Identifier of the item the gripper now holds. It repeats the goal's identifier, or names one the implementer minted for an item the goal addressed by pose, so the held item is always addressable afterwards." },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s), whatever the outcome." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unknown_frame", "no_chain", "extrapolation", "broken_tree"],
        marks: ["moves_robot", "reaches_for_item"],
      },
      {
        name: "drop_item",
        description: "Open one gripper and release the item that it holds: where the gripper stands, or, with target_item_id, above that item, which the implementer carries the held item over before the jaws open, with no descent. The implementer forgets the released item, as after each drop. The feedback gives each stage of the drop as it starts. With a target item: plan, while the implementer looks for a path above it; move_above, the carry of the held item above it; with a model that aligns the gripper, align_look and align_move, as grab_item gives them; then release, the opening of the jaws. With none, or with jaws that hold nothing to carry: release alone. The result tells whether the release succeeded, and names the gripper and the released item. All other fields except action_time are zero or empty when success is false.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            gripper_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Which gripper releases, named from the implementer's fixed set of gripper names. Empty means the gripper currently holding an item; refused in the result when none or more than one holds. An unknown name is refused in the result, as is a gripper holding nothing. With no target_item_id the item is released where the gripper already is; place_item carries it somewhere first." },
            target_item_id: { $type: "string", $optional: true, $marks: ["item_id"], $description: "Identifier of the item to drop the held item into, such as a bowl: the implementer carries the held item above it and opens the jaws there with no descent. Absent or empty: the gripper opens where it stands. Refused in the result before any move when the implementer no longer recognises the identifier, when it names the held item itself or an item another gripper holds, and when the implementer cannot reach above the item." },
          },
        },
        feedback_topic: {
          qos_profile: "reliable",
          message_format: {
            stage: { $type: "string", $enum: ["plan", "move_above", "align_look", "align_move", "release"], $description: "The stage that starts now, as the description of the action names it." },
            activity: { $type: "string", $marks: ["activity"], $description: "One sentence for the person who looks at the robot: what the robot does now, in the words of what that person sees (the robot, its arm, its hand, each item by its label), with no name of a link, a joint, a contract or a model and no term of the motion planner. A stage that repeats ends the sentence with its number and its maximum, as \"(2 of 5)\", so the sentence alone tells one repeat from the next." },
            number: { $type: "u32", $description: "The number of this repeat of a stage that repeats, from 1. For align_look and align_move, the step of the alignment, which a question to the model and the correction that its answer gives share: a step whose answer moves nothing gives no align_move. 0 for a stage that does not repeat." },
            maximum: { $type: "u32", $description: "How many times the stage can repeat in this goal: for align_look and align_move, the steps of the alignment. 0 for a stage that does not repeat." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            success: { $type: "bool", $description: "False when the release was refused, failed, cancelled, or aborted; message says which. Refused before releasing when another sequence is running, the named gripper is unknown or holds nothing, the name is empty while no gripper or more than one holds, or the target_item_id is unknown, names the held item or an item another gripper holds, or is out of reach." },
            message: "string",
            gripper_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Gripper that released the item, from the implementer's fixed set of gripper names." },
            item_id: { $type: "string", $marks: ["item_id"], $description: "Identifier of the item that was released, as grab_item reported it." },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s), whatever the outcome." },
          },
        },
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
      {
        name: "place_item",
        description: "Carry the item that one gripper holds to a pose, or into or onto a target item named by target_item_id, and release it there. With a target item, the implementer carries the held item above the target item, picks the free spot, lowers the item until it rests and opens the jaws, then climbs back: after a place the arm stands above where the item went and can hide that spot from the camera. The target item keeps its identifier. The feedback gives each stage of the place as it starts: plan, while the implementer looks for a path above the pose or the target item; move_above, the carry of the held item there; with a model that aligns the gripper, align_look and align_move, as grab_item gives them; then set_down, the descent until the item rests, the opening of the jaws and the climb back. The result tells whether the placement succeeded, and gives the gripper, the placed item and where the measured grasp point stood when the jaws opened. All other fields except action_time are zero or empty when success is false, and final_point is absent.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            gripper_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Which gripper carries and releases the item, named from the implementer's fixed set of gripper names. Empty means the gripper currently holding an item; refused in the result when none or more than one holds. An unknown name is refused in the result, as is a gripper holding nothing." },
            target: {
              $type: "object",
              $description: "The grasp-point pose when the jaws open, given in frame at timestamp. It is where the gripper lets go, not a waypoint on the way there. The implementer lowers the item to it and, when the item comes to rest on something on the way, lets go there instead: final_point says where the jaws opened. A target with no orientation leaves the orientation to the implementer, which is what a caller means when it cares where the item ends up and not which way it faces. Not read when the goal names a target_item_id; a goal that names one sends a zero position here, with no frame, no timestamp and no orientation.",
              frame: { $type: "string", $optional: true, $description: "The frame of the record's values, as transforms names frames; absent, the robot frame." },
              timestamp: { $type: "time", $optional: true, $description: "The time on the clock of transforms at which the values hold. A command leaves it out for the latest time; a report leaves it out for values that hold at every time." },
              position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "x, y, z (m)." },
              orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $optional: true, $description: "A unit quaternion [x, y, z, w], or absent for none." },
            },
            target_item_id: { $type: "string", $optional: true, $marks: ["item_id"], $description: "Identifier of the item to put the held item in or on, such as a bowl or a tray, from item_perception: the implementer carries the held item above it, picks the free spot, lowers the item until it rests on the target item or on what the target item holds, and opens there. target is not read. Absent or empty: the place goes to target. Refused in the result before any move when the implementer no longer recognises the identifier, when it names the held item itself or an item another gripper holds, and when the implementer cannot reach the target item." },
          },
        },
        feedback_topic: {
          qos_profile: "reliable",
          message_format: {
            stage: { $type: "string", $enum: ["plan", "move_above", "align_look", "align_move", "set_down"], $description: "The stage that starts now, as the description of the action names it." },
            activity: { $type: "string", $marks: ["activity"], $description: "One sentence for the person who looks at the robot: what the robot does now, in the words of what that person sees (the robot, its arm, its hand, each item by its label), with no name of a link, a joint, a contract or a model and no term of the motion planner. A stage that repeats ends the sentence with its number and its maximum, as \"(2 of 5)\", so the sentence alone tells one repeat from the next." },
            number: { $type: "u32", $description: "The number of this repeat of a stage that repeats, from 1. For align_look and align_move, the step of the alignment, which a question to the model and the correction that its answer gives share: a step whose answer moves nothing gives no align_move. 0 for a stage that does not repeat." },
            maximum: { $type: "u32", $description: "How many times the stage can repeat in this goal: for align_look and align_move, the steps of the alignment. 0 for a stage that does not repeat." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            success: { $type: "bool", $description: "False when the placement was refused, failed, cancelled, or aborted; message says which. Refused before carrying when another sequence is running, the named gripper is unknown or holds nothing, the name is empty while no gripper or more than one holds, the target_item_id is unknown, names the held item or an item another gripper holds, or the target pose or the target item is one the implementer cannot reach, which it refuses rather than approximates." },
            message: "string",
            gripper_name: { $type: "string", $description: "Gripper that placed the item, from the implementer's fixed set of gripper names." },
            item_id: { $type: "string", $marks: ["item_id"], $description: "Identifier of the item that was placed, as grab_item reported it." },
            final_point: {
              $type: "object",
              $optional: true,
              $description: "Where the measured grasp point stood when the jaws opened, in the robot frame, at the time of that measurement. Absent when success is false.",
              frame: { $type: "string", $description: "The frame of the record's values, as transforms names frames." },
              timestamp: { $type: "time", $description: "The time on the clock of transforms at which the values hold." },
              position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "x, y, z (m)." },
            },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s), whatever the outcome." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unknown_frame", "no_chain", "extrapolation", "broken_tree"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
      {
        name: "abort",
        description: "Stop the sequence that runs now, whoever started it, and return once the robot has come to rest, standing where the stop left it. The action gives no feedback. The result names the action that was stopped, empty when no sequence was running.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            reason: { $type: "string", $description: "Why the sequence is being stopped, recorded by the implementer alongside the abort. Empty is accepted." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            success: { $type: "bool", $description: "False only when the abort itself could not be carried out; message says why. An abort with no sequence running succeeds." },
            message: "string",
            aborted_action: { $type: "string", $description: "Name of the action that was stopped, as it appears in this contract. Empty when no sequence was running." },
            action_time: { $type: "f64", $description: "Wall-clock duration of the action (s), whatever the outcome." },
          },
        },
      },
    ],
    services: [
      {
        name: "get_state",
        description: "Give what the implementer is doing and what it is holding, as of this call. It answers \"is action X being performed?\" by comparing X against current_action, \"is the robot holding an item?\" from the held flags, and \"are the jaws still on it?\" from the measured openings.",
        response_message_format: {
          current_action: { $type: "string", $description: "Name of the sequence running now, as it appears in this contract (e.g. \"grab_item\"). Empty when no sequence is running, which is also when a new goal is accepted." },
          current_action_elapsed_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "How long the running sequence has been going (s). 0 when none is running." },
          gripper_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The implementer's fixed set of gripper names, in a stable order. holding, held_item_ids and gripper_openings carry one entry per gripper in this order." },
          holding: { $type: "array", $items: "bool", $description: "True where that gripper holds an item." },
          held_item_ids: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $marks: ["item_id"], $description: "Identifier of the item that gripper holds, addressable by drop_item and place_item. Empty where holding is false." },
          gripper_openings: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Measured opening fraction of that gripper (0 = closed, 1 = fully open), as the implementer last measured it: what the jaws do now, whatever the held flag says. Empty, not one entry per gripper, while the implementer has no measurement of every gripper." },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
}
